{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"convention|review|test.author|immutab|commit order|full suite|builder\\\" conformance roles ci README.md .github 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"ci/rollback-drill.md:9:3. The revert PR goes through CI like any change (fast — no review rounds needed for a pure revert; the operator approves directly).\nci/test-immutability-check.sh:2:# test-immutability-check.sh — CI gate enforcing two mechanical rules that\nci/test-immutability-check.sh:8:#   mixing both fails: that is a builder bundling test edits with code.\nci/test-immutability-check.sh:14:# A builder pushing a late test-only commit is caught by Rule 2. The reviewer\nci/test-immutability-check.sh:71:  echo \"test immutability holds: test commits are pure and all precede implementation ($TEST_PATHS)\"\nci/github-actions-ci.template.yml:25:  test-immutability:\nci/github-actions-ci.template.yml:31:      - name: builder commits must not touch tests\nci/github-actions-ci.template.yml:32:        run: .github/scripts/test-immutability-check.sh\nci/github-actions-ci.template.yml:38:# \"test-immutability\" (see ci/branch-protection.md).\nci/branch-protection.md:10:- Required status checks: `ci` and `test-immutability`, strict (branch up to date).\nci/branch-protection.md:13:- Required approving reviews: 1 once the org has ≥2 humans. At single-operator stage set it to 0 — GitHub forbids approving your own PR, so a sole human with a 1-review rule can never merge anything. Merge-by-operator stays mechanical anyway: deploy keys cannot merge PRs (git-only credential), and `main` rejects their direct pushes.\nci/branch-protection.md:14:- No merge queue at single-builder stage — it queues nothing; add it only when concurrency arrives.\nci/branch-protection.md:26:    { \"type\": \"pull_request\", \"parameters\": { \"required_approving_review_count\": 0, \"dismiss_stale_reviews_on_push\": false, \"require_code_owner_review\": false, \"require_last_push_approval\": false, \"required_review_thread_resolution\": false, \"allowed_merge_methods\": [\"merge\", \"squash\"] } },\nci/branch-protection.md:27:    { \"type\": \"required_status_checks\", \"parameters\": { \"strict_required_status_checks_policy\": true, \"required_status_checks\": [ { \"context\": \"ci\" }, { \"context\": \"test-immutability\" } ] } },\nroles/builder.md:5:You implement one spec'd ticket in a fresh git worktree until the test-author's tests pass. You cannot merge, you cannot edit tests, and you cannot change specs or contracts.\nroles/builder.md:9:The ticket (spec, acceptance criteria, frozen contract) and the branch containing the test-author's failing tests.\nroles/builder.md:17:- **Never touch test files.** CI fails the PR mechanically if your commits modify test paths; don't fight it. If a test looks wrong, say so on the ticket and stop — the reviewer adjudicates.\nroles/builder.md:19:- Follow the conventions doc. Smallest change that satisfies the tests; no drive-by refactors, no new dependencies without a ticket note explaining why.\nci/railway.md:3:Railway hosts staging, PR preview deploys, and Postgres. Chosen over Fly.io for a non-technical operator: no Dockerfile required, built-in Postgres with automated backups, deploys from GitHub pushes.\nci/railway.md:9:3. Enable PR environments: Settings → Environments → enable \"PR environments\" (this is the preview deploy the Narrator screenshots).\nci/railway.md:15:- `main` branch → staging environment. PRs → ephemeral preview environments.\n.github/workflows/ci.yml:23:  test-immutability:\n.github/workflows/ci.yml:29:      - name: builder commits must not touch tests\n.github/workflows/ci.yml:30:        run: bash ci/test-immutability-check.sh\nREADME.md:3:A product-agnostic kit for running an AI software factory: agents plan, build, review, and document work on a Linear board; a human sets priorities and approves from evidence bundles, never from diffs.\nREADME.md:13:| `roles/` | Versioned prompt files for the five roles (planner, test-author, builder, reviewer, narrator) |\nREADME.md:16:| `ci/` | Test-immutability check, branch protection, walking-skeleton pattern, rollback drill, Railway recipe |\nREADME.md:24:2. The builder cannot edit tests — CI fails the PR if builder commits touch test files.\nREADME.md:26:4. Test author and reviewer run on a different model family than the builder.\nREADME.md:27:5. Two review rounds, then the ticket escalates to a human with a plain-language note.\nconformance/factory/runs/1783912071-74583.out:2:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":128911,\"duration_api_ms\":122302,\"ttft_ms\":2032,\"ttft_stream_ms\":1549,\"time_to_request_ms\":173,\"num_turns\":24,\"result\":\"## Summary\\n\\nImplemented the frozen contract exactly: `/health` in `conformance/app/server.js` now returns an `approvals` object counting `state.approvals` by status (`pending`/`sent`/`rejected`/`blocked_recipient`), alongside the unchanged `ok`/`queue` fields.\\n\\n**Result: not fully green — stopping to flag a contract conflict, not committing over it.**\\n\\n- `tests/health-approvals.test.js` (test-author's frozen contract tests, commit `18a7731`): **3/3 pass**, exact `JSON.stringify` match on all three acceptance criteria.\\n- `tests/health.test.js` (pre-existing T-101 tests): **4/4 fail.** They use `assert.deepStrictEqual` against object literals with no `approvals` key, and `deepStrictEqual` rejects any extra key. Since the frozen contract requires `approvals` to always be present on `/health`, no implementation can satisfy the contract *and* keep these particular assertions green — they were written before this contract existed and don't tolerate additive fields.\\n- `tests/conformance.test.js`: unaffected (only checks `response.ok`).\\n\\nThis is a genuine ticket/test conflict, not a bug in my implementation, so per the builder rules I didn't touch any test file or improvise a workaround. I logged the finding in detail on `conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md` and committed the implementation + ticket note (commit `5e201e0`) — no test files were modified. This needs reviewer/planner adjudication: either `health.test.js` gets updated by the test-author to tolerate the new key, or the contract is revisited.\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"97cd656a-9590-4cc1-9f7a-b5bd30255c88\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.6861495,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":44,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":37851,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1102495,\"output_tokens\":8498,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":37851,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":2,\"output_tokens\":547,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":60415,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":646,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":646},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":608,\"outputTokens\":17,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.000693,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-5\":{\"inputTokens\":44,\"outputTokens\":8498,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1102495,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":37851,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.6854564999999999,\"contextWindow\":1000000,\"maxOutputTokens\":64000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"e0ab248a-d2fd-4f8e-a554-6538a2f2d719\"}\nroles/narrator.md:5:You produce the evidence bundle the operator approves from. The operator cannot read code; your bundle is their only quality lens. It is produced **before merge**, from the PR's preview deploy.\nroles/narrator.md:9:The approved-by-reviewer PR, its preview deploy URL, the ticket, CI results, and the run-cost ledger entries for this ticket.\nroles/narrator.md:14:2. **Preview link** to click, with a one-line \"what to try\".\nroles/narrator.md:27:- If the preview deploy is broken, the bundle is one line: preview broken, not approvable, and the ticket goes back to the builder.\nci/walking-skeleton.md:14:4. The PR gets a preview deploy; merge deploys to staging.\nroles/reviewer.md:5:You review the builder's diff for what machines cannot check: test adequacy and spec conformance. You run on a different model family than the builder, and you never write code.\nroles/reviewer.md:9:The PR (diff, description), the ticket (spec, acceptance criteria, frozen contract), the conventions doc, and the CI results.\nroles/reviewer.md:13:1. **Do the tests actually test the acceptance criteria?** Not \"do they pass\" — CI knows that. Would they catch a wrong implementation? Is any criterion untested? Did the builder's implementation dodge the intent while satisfying the letter?\nroles/reviewer.md:14:2. **Does the change conform to the spec and conventions?** Contract respected exactly, no invented behavior, no scope creep, docs updated where the change made them false.\nroles/reviewer.md:18:Either **Approve** (one comment: what you checked and why it passes) or **Request changes** (numbered, actionable items tied to a criterion or convention — never taste).\nroles/reviewer.md:28:Receipt-row PR: reviewer notices the test asserts a row exists but never checks the irreversible-action case (criterion 3), and the builder hard-coded `reversible: true`. Request changes, round 1, item 1: \"Criterion 3 untested and unimplemented: irreversible actions must show no Undo control; current code hard-codes reversible: true.\"\nroles/planner.md:9:A Linear ticket the operator has moved to Ready, plus the product docs: engine spec, acceptance spec, conventions, and the current codebase.\nroles/planner.md:15:3. **Frozen contract**: the exact interface both the test-author and the builder code against — endpoint paths and shapes, UI selectors, fixture data, file locations. Once posted, the contract does not change; if it proves wrong, the ticket goes back to Ready and you re-plan it as a new version, noted on the ticket.\nroles/planner.md:19:- A ticket too big for one builder session gets split into linked tickets, each with its own contract.\nroles/test-author.md:5:You write the failing acceptance tests for a spec'd ticket, before the builder starts. You run on a different model family than the builder, and you never write implementation code.\nroles/test-author.md:13:- Failing tests, committed as the **first commits on the ticket branch**, in the test paths defined by the product's conventions doc.\nroles/README.md:1:# Roles — versioning convention\nroles/README.md:7:- **Cross-family rule.** Builder runs on model family A (Claude). Test-author and reviewer run on family B (Codex/OpenAI). Never collapse them onto one family — independent judgment is the point.\nroles/README.md:8:- **Prompts are not enforcement.** Anything that must be true (budgets, test immutability, merge rights) is enforced by the wrapper, CI, or repo permissions. Prompts describe the job; mechanics enforce the rules.\nconformance/factory/runs/1783912838-78570.out:2:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":177175,\"duration_api_ms\":165859,\"ttft_ms\":2156,\"ttft_stream_ms\":1427,\"time_to_request_ms\":249,\"num_turns\":24,\"result\":\"Committed as `5e3838b` on `ticket/T-102-health-approvals-summary`.\\n\\nThe bundle at `conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md` covers:\\n\\n- **What changed**: `/health` now also reports approvals counts (pending/sent/rejected/blocked_recipient) alongside T-101's existing queue counts.\\n- **Escalation**: the builder found that the frozen contract necessarily breaks 4 pre-existing T-101 exact-match test assertions, correctly declined to edit tests or paper over it, and escalated. Traced through all three rounds — operator's contract-stands decision, two dispatcher-level sequencer/bookkeeping escalations, reviewer round 1 (REQUEST CHANGES) → test-author fix → reviewer round 2 (APPROVE).\\n- **Test evidence**: before (11 passed / 4 failed, all in `health.test.js`) vs. after — I re-ran the full suite live just now and confirmed 15/15 green.\\n- **Commit list**: all 15 T-102 commits with descriptions.\\n- **Cost table**: all 6 completed ledger rows ($1.7169747 total) plus the narrator's reserved $1.50 flagged as a budget hold, not final spend.\\n- **Acceptance criteria**: AC1–AC3 each verified against a live local demo (no preview deploy exists yet for this project, same gap noted in the T-101 bundle) with exact JSON responses matching the frozen contract.\\n- **Risk**: internal/low per the evidence rubric, with rollback via reverting the three implementation/test commits (or the eventual PR).\\n\\nNo product code, tests, or the frozen contract were touched — only the new bundle file was added.\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"6ae515d2-ebb7-4a54-8b68-50d90e6622b7\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.8123735,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":38,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":48210,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1031145,\"output_tokens\":14192,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":48210,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":2,\"output_tokens\":573,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":70889,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":531,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":531},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":676,\"outputTokens\":20,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.000776,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-5\":{\"inputTokens\":38,\"outputTokens\":14192,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1031145,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":48210,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.8115974999999999,\"contextWindow\":1000000,\"maxOutputTokens\":64000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"6d4c9f42-5677-4050-9db1-c770ac2682bc\"}\nconformance/factory/ENVELOPE.env:4:# - test-author (codex): $0.35\nconformance/factory/ENVELOPE.env:5:# - builder (claude) attempt 1: $0.69, hard-stopped by --max-budget-usd at the\nconformance/factory/ENVELOPE.env:7:# - builder attempt 2: $1.48 (green, committed)\nconformance/factory/ENVELOPE.env:9:# reviewer run at $2.52 spent + $1.50 reserve — the refusal itself was correct\nroles/dispatcher.md:20:Role runs launched in the sequence defined by `workflows/ticket-flow.md` (planner → test-author → builder → reviewer → narrator), ticket state moves with logged reasons, and escalations. Nothing else.\nroles/dispatcher.md:25:- **The sequencer picks the stage, not you.** Before every launch, run `scripts/next-stage.sh --ticket <T-NNN>` and do what it says (`RUN <role>`, `FIX` — where you pick test-author vs builder from the reviewer's feedback — `AWAIT-OPERATOR`, `ESCALATE`, or `REFUSE`). If it refuses because a reviewer verdict is unrecorded, record the verdict line on the ticket first (`reviewer round N: APPROVE` / `reviewer round N: REQUEST CHANGES — reason`); never launch against its output.\nroles/dispatcher.md:27:- **Never merge, never approve.** Merges happen only through the operator's approval on the Narrator's evidence bundle. You may open the PR on the builder's behalf if it hasn't been opened; you never approve or merge it.\nroles/dispatcher.md:29:- **Two-round review limit.** After the reviewer's second REQUEST CHANGES on the same ticket, escalate instead of launching more rounds.\nroles/dispatcher.md:36:Ticket T-102 sits in Ready. Correct dispatch: launch planner via the wrapper; when it posts spec + branch, move to In progress with log line \"planner done, contract v1 posted\". Launch test-author; on its commit, launch builder in a fresh worktree; on green, launch reviewer. Reviewer replies REQUEST CHANGES — launch test-author round 2 with the reviewer's feedback in the task text, then reviewer round 2. On APPROVE, launch narrator; when the bundle is posted, move the ticket to Review with log line \"bundle posted, awaiting operator\" and stop. If instead the wrapper had refused the builder run with a ticket-budget message, the correct move is Blocked-Escalated with that exact message — not a retry, not an envelope edit.\nroles/dispatcher.md:41:- v2: stage selection moved from judgment to mechanism — `scripts/next-stage.sh` is now mandatory before every launch; reviewer verdicts must be recorded on the ticket file (the sequencer blocks until they are).\nconformance/factory/runs/1783866358-36047.out:1:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":79847,\"duration_api_ms\":76393,\"ttft_ms\":5954,\"ttft_stream_ms\":4411,\"time_to_request_ms\":77,\"num_turns\":8,\"result\":\"Bundle written to `conformance/factory/tickets/T-101-bundle.md`. TLDR for you:\\n\\n- **Demo ran live and passed**: on a fresh local server, `/health` returned `{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"queue\\\":{\\\"pending\\\":0,\\\"done\\\":0,\\\"dead\\\":0}}`; after posting one webhook event it showed `pending: 1`, then `done: 1` two seconds later. Real captured JSON is in the bundle; server was killed afterward.\\n- **All 3 acceptance criteria PASS** — criteria 1 and 2 by both tests and live demo, criterion 3 (dead-job count after retries exhaust) by test `3.` in `tests/health.test.js`. Gates: health tests 4/4, conformance suite 8/8, immutability green, reviewer APPROVE (round 2).\\n- **Risk**: low, internal read-only change; nothing sent externally, no data changed.\\n- **Cost**: ~$4.30 total for the ticket (test-author $0.35, builder $2.17 across 2 attempts, reviewer $0.98 across 2 rounds, narrator ~$0.80 estimated).\\n- **Rollback**: revert single commit `aa6adc9`.\\n\\nThe bundle ends with the operator question: approve to merge, or send back. Note it says the demo was local since no preview deploy exists yet — Linear posting wasn't done (Linear MCP isn't authenticated in this session, and I wouldn't post without your go-ahead anyway).\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"a04f4e3c-79b8-4642-bf59-8514eec433cd\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.9962,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":74,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":27423,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":295850,\"output_tokens\":3023,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":27423,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":2,\"output_tokens\":26,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":42325,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1448,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1448},\"type\":\"message\"},{\"input_tokens\":60,\"output_tokens\":490,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":43773,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-fable-5\":{\"inputTokens\":74,\"outputTokens\":3023,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":295850,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":27423,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.9962,\"contextWindow\":1000000,\"maxOutputTokens\":64000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"85ea03ad-e65f-457b-b81e-aa5d4a41cdc6\"}\nconformance/factory/ENVELOPE.md:12:Retries/escalation: 2 reviewer rounds; 2 builder attempts; then Blocked-Escalated. External actions: Relay's allowlist is `test@example.com` only — production mode does not exist in this product by design.\nconformance/factory/runs/1783866071-31885.out:5:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’m using the active Ponytail workflow: I’ll inspect the ticket, conventions, current test, and callers first, then make only the two requested test strengthenings.\"}}\nconformance/factory/runs/1783866071-31885.out:6:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"pwd && rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*conventions*' -g 'T-101.md' -g 'health.test.js' -g 'conformance.test.js' -g 'package.json' && git status --short && sed -n '1,240p' conformance/factory/tickets/T-101.md && sed -n '1,260p' conformance/app/tests/health.test.js && sed -n '1,220p' conformance/app/package.json\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\nconformance/factory/runs/1783866071-31885.out:7:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"pwd && rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*conventions*' -g 'T-101.md' -g 'health.test.js' -g 'conformance.test.js' -g 'package.json' && git status --short && sed -n '1,240p' conformance/factory/tickets/T-101.md && sed -n '1,260p' conformance/app/tests/health.test.js && sed -n '1,220p' conformance/app/package.json\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"/Users/javieraldape/Projects/sf-worktrees/T-101\\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-101.md\\nconformance/app/package.json\\nconformance/app/tests/conformance.test.js\\nconformance/app/tests/health.test.js\\n# T-101 — /health reports queue depth\\n\\nState: In progress\\nBranch: ticket/T-101-health-queue-depth\\nRisk class: low (read-only endpoint, no external actions)\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nOperators need one glance to see whether Relay's job queue is healthy. Extend the existing `GET /health` endpoint to report how many jobs are pending, done, and dead.\\n\\n## Frozen contract (v1)\\n\\n`GET /health` returns HTTP 200 with JSON:\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"queue\\\": { \\\"pending\\\": 0, \\\"done\\\": 0, \\\"dead\\\": 0 } }\\n```\\n\\n- `ok` keeps its current meaning and stays `true` whenever the server responds.\\n- `queue.pending`, `queue.done`, `queue.dead` are integer counts of jobs in `state.jobs` by their `status` field.\\n- No other endpoint changes. No new endpoints.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n1. On a fresh server (no events), `/health` returns `ok: true` and `queue: { pending: 0, done: 0, dead: 0 }`.\\n2. After an event is accepted and its job completes, `/health` reports `queue.done` incremented by 1.\\n3. After an event whose payload sets `failTimes: 99` exhausts retries, `/health` reports `queue.dead` incremented by 1.\\n\\n## Conventions\\n\\n- App lives in `conformance/app/` (zero-dependency Node 18+; see `conformance/SPEC.md`).\\n- Tests go in `conformance/app/tests/` — new file `tests/health.test.js`, same style as `conformance.test.js` (node:test, spawn the real server).\\n- Run tests from `conformance/app/` with `node --test tests/health.test.js`.\\n\\n## Log\\n\\n- 2026-07-12: spec + frozen contract posted (planner step performed by the operator's assistant for this first calibration ticket). Tests written: pending. Build: pending. Review: pending. Bundle: pending.\\nconst { test, before, after } = require(\\\"node:test\\\");\\nconst assert = require(\\\"node:assert\\\");\\nconst { spawn } = require(\\\"node:child_process\\\");\\nconst fs = require(\\\"node:fs\\\");\\nconst path = require(\\\"node:path\\\");\\nconst os = require(\\\"node:os\\\");\\n\\nconst PORT = 4721;\\nconst BASE = `http://localhost:${PORT}`;\\nconst DATA_DIR = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \\\"relay-health-test-\\\"));\\nconst SERVER = path.join(__dirname, \\\"..\\\", \\\"server.js\\\");\\nlet proc;\\n\\nconst post = (body) => fetch(`${BASE}/webhook/event`, {\\n  method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n  headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n  body: JSON.stringify(body),\\n});\\nconst getHealth = async () => (await fetch(`${BASE}/health`)).json();\\nconst getState = async () => (await fetch(`${BASE}/api/state`)).json();\\n\\nasync function settle(pred, tries = 60) {\\n  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {\\n    const state = await getState();\\n    if (pred(state)) return;\\n    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\\n  }\\n  throw new Error(\\\"job did not settle\\\");\\n}\\n\\nbefore(async () => {\\n  proc = spawn(process.execPath, [SERVER], {\\n    env: { ...process.env, PORT: String(PORT), DATA_DIR, WORKER_MS: \\\"50\\\" },\\n    stdio: \\\"ignore\\\",\\n  });\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\\n    try {\\n      if ((await fetch(`${BASE}/health`)).ok) return;\\n    } catch { /* not up yet */ }\\n    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\\n  }\\n  throw new Error(\\\"server did not come up\\\");\\n});\\n\\nafter(() => {\\n  proc?.kill(\\\"SIGKILL\\\");\\n  fs.rmSync(DATA_DIR, { recursive: true, force: true });\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"1. on a fresh server, /health reports an empty queue\\\", async () => {\\n  assert.deepStrictEqual(await getHealth(), {\\n    ok: true,\\n    queue: { pending: 0, done: 0, dead: 0 },\\n  });\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"2. after a job completes, /health reports queue.done incremented by 1\\\", async () => {\\n  await post({ id: \\\"health-done\\\", payload: {} });\\n  await settle(state => state.jobs.find(job => job.eventId === \\\"health-done\\\")?.status === \\\"done\\\");\\n\\n  assert.deepStrictEqual(await getHealth(), {\\n    ok: true,\\n    queue: { pending: 0, done: 1, dead: 0 },\\n  });\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"3. after a job exhausts retries, /health reports queue.dead incremented by 1\\\", async () => {\\n  await post({ id: \\\"health-dead\\\", payload: { failTimes: 99 } });\\n  await settle(state => state.jobs.find(job => job.eventId === \\\"health-dead\\\")?.status === \\\"dead\\\");\\n\\n  assert.deepStrictEqual(await getHealth(), {\\n    ok: true,\\n    queue: { pending: 0, done: 1, dead: 1 },\\n  });\\n});\\n{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"relay-conformance\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Nysa-shaped conformance product for the software factory kit. Zero dependencies.\\\",\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"start\\\": \\\"node server.js\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"node --test tests/conformance.test.js\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\nconformance/factory/runs/1783866071-31885.out:10:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,320p' conformance/app/server.js && sed -n '1,280p' conformance/app/tests/conformance.test.js && git log --oneline -8 -- conformance/app/tests/health.test.js && git branch --show-current && git status --porcelain=v1\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"// Relay — conformance product. Zero dependencies; Node 18+.\\n// See ../SPEC.md for the behavior contract this implements.\\nconst http = require(\\\"node:http\\\");\\nconst fs = require(\\\"node:fs\\\");\\nconst path = require(\\\"node:path\\\");\\nconst crypto = require(\\\"node:crypto\\\");\\n\\nconst PORT = Number(process.env.PORT || 4700);\\nconst DATA_DIR = process.env.DATA_DIR || path.join(__dirname, \\\"data\\\");\\nconst STATE_FILE = path.join(DATA_DIR, \\\"state.json\\\");\\nconst ALLOWLIST = (process.env.ALLOWLIST || \\\"test@example.com\\\").split(\\\",\\\").map(s => s.trim());\\nconst WORKER_MS = Number(process.env.WORKER_MS || 200);\\nconst MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3;\\n\\n// ---------- durable state ----------\\nlet state = { events: [], jobs: [], approvals: [], outbox: [] };\\n\\nfunction loadState() {\\n  try {\\n    state = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(STATE_FILE, \\\"utf8\\\"));\\n  } catch {\\n    /* first boot or unreadable: start clean */\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Atomic persist: write temp file, then rename. A crash mid-write never\\n// corrupts the previous good state.\\nfunction persist() {\\n  fs.mkdirSync(DATA_DIR, { recursive: true });\\n  const tmp = STATE_FILE + \\\".\\\" + crypto.randomBytes(4).toString(\\\"hex\\\");\\n  fs.writeFileSync(tmp, JSON.stringify(state, null, 2));\\n  fs.renameSync(tmp, STATE_FILE);\\n}\\n\\n// ---------- domain ----------\\nfunction acceptEvent(evt) {\\n  if (!evt || typeof evt.id !== \\\"string\\\" || !evt.id) return { ok: false, error: \\\"missing event id\\\" };\\n  const existing = state.events.find(e => e.id === evt.id);\\n  if (existing) return { ok: true, duplicate: true, eventId: evt.id }; // idempotent ack\\n  state.events.push({ id: evt.id, type: evt.type || \\\"generic\\\", payload: evt.payload || {}, receivedAt: new Date().toISOString() });\\n  state.jobs.push({\\n    id: \\\"job-\\\" + evt.id,\\n    eventId: evt.id,\\n    status: \\\"pending\\\", // pending | done | dead\\n    attempts: 0,\\n    lastError: null,\\n  });\\n  persist();\\n  return { ok: true, duplicate: false, eventId: evt.id };\\n}\\n\\nfunction processJob(job) {\\n  const evt = state.events.find(e => e.id === job.eventId);\\n  job.attempts += 1;\\n  // Simulated transient/permanent failure: payload.failTimes = number of\\n  // attempts that must fail before success (99 = effectively permanent).\\n  const failTimes = Number(evt?.payload?.failTimes || 0);\\n  if (job.attempts <= failTimes) {\\n    job.lastError = `simulated failure on attempt ${job.attempts}`;\\n    if (job.attempts >= MAX_ATTEMPTS) job.status = \\\"dead\\\";\\n    persist();\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  // Success: produce a proposed action requiring approval. Nothing sends here.\\n  state.approvals.push({\\n    id: \\\"appr-\\\" + job.eventId,\\n    jobId: job.id,\\n    action: {\\n      to: evt?.payload?.to || ALLOWLIST[0],\\n      subject: evt?.payload?.subject || `Follow-up for ${job.eventId}`,\\n      body: evt?.payload?.body || \\\"Proposed by Relay worker.\\\",\\n    },\\n    status: \\\"pending\\\", // pending | sent | rejected | blocked_recipient\\n    proposedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\\n  });\\n  job.status = \\\"done\\\";\\n  job.lastError = null;\\n  persist();\\n}\\n\\nfunction workerTick() {\\n  const job = state.jobs.find(j => j.status === \\\"pending\\\");\\n  if (job) processJob(job);\\n}\\n\\nfunction approve(id) {\\n  const appr = state.approvals.find(a => a.id === id);\\n  if (!appr) return { ok: false, code: 404, error: \\\"no such approval\\\" };\\n  if (appr.status !== \\\"pending\\\") return { ok: false, code: 409, error: `already ${appr.status}` };\\n  if (!ALLOWLIST.includes(appr.action.to)) {\\n    appr.status = \\\"blocked_recipient\\\";\\n    persist();\\n    return { ok: false, code: 403, error: `recipient ${appr.action.to} not on allowlist — send blocked`, status: appr.status };\\n  }\\n  state.outbox.push({ ...appr.action, approvalId: appr.id, sentAt: new Date().toISOString() });\\n  appr.status = \\\"sent\\\";\\n  persist();\\n  return { ok: true, status: \\\"sent\\\" };\\n}\\n\\nfunction reject(id) {\\n  const appr = state.approvals.find(a => a.id === id);\\n  if (!appr) return { ok: false, code: 404, error: \\\"no such approval\\\" };\\n  if (appr.status !== \\\"pending\\\") return { ok: false, code: 409, error: `already ${appr.status}` };\\n  appr.status = \\\"rejected\\\";\\n  persist();\\n  return { ok: true, status: \\\"rejected\\\" };\\n}\\n\\n// ---------- http ----------\\nfunction json(res, code, obj) {\\n  res.writeHead(code, { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" });\\n  res.end(JSON.stringify(obj));\\n}\\n\\nfunction readBody(req) {\\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n    let data = \\\"\\\";\\n    req.on(\\\"data\\\", c => { data += c; if (data.length > 1e6) req.destroy(); });\\n    req.on(\\\"end\\\", () => { try { resolve(data ? JSON.parse(data) : {}); } catch (e) { reject(e); } });\\n    req.on(\\\"error\\\", reject);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nfunction ui() {\\n  const row = (cells) => `<tr>${cells.map(c => `<td>${String(c)}</td>`).join(\\\"\\\")}</tr>`;\\n  return `<!doctype html><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\"><title>Relay</title>\\n<style>body{font-family:system-ui;margin:2rem;max-width:60rem}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:1.5rem}td,th{border:1px solid #ddd;padding:.4rem .6rem;text-align:left;font-size:14px}h2{margin:.2rem 0 .4rem}</style>\\n<h1>Relay</h1>\\n<h2>Events (${state.events.length})</h2><table><tr><th>id</th><th>type</th><th>received</th></tr>${state.events.map(e => row([e.id, e.type, e.receivedAt])).join(\\\"\\\")}</table>\\n<h2>Jobs</h2><table><tr><th>id</th><th>status</th><th>attempts</th><th>lastError</th></tr>${state.jobs.map(j => row([j.id, j.status, j.attempts, j.lastError || \\\"\\\"])).join(\\\"\\\")}</table>\\n<h2>Approvals</h2><table><tr><th>id</th><th>to</th><th>subject</th><th>status</th></tr>${state.approvals.map(a => row([a.id, a.action.to, a.action.subject, a.status])).join(\\\"\\\")}</table>\\n<h2>Outbox (sandboxed)</h2><table><tr><th>to</th><th>subject</th><th>sentAt</th></tr>${state.outbox.map(o => row([o.to, o.subject, o.sentAt])).join(\\\"\\\")}</table>`;\\n}\\n\\nconst server = http.createServer(async (req, res) => {\\n  const url = new URL(req.url, `http://localhost:${PORT}`);\\n  try {\\n    if (req.method === \\\"GET\\\" && url.pathname === \\\"/\\\") {\\n      res.writeHead(200, { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"text/html\\\" });\\n      return res.end(ui());\\n    }\\n    if (req.method === \\\"GET\\\" && url.pathname === \\\"/api/state\\\") return json(res, 200, state);\\n    if (req.method === \\\"GET\\\" && url.pathname === \\\"/health\\\") {\\n      const queue = { pending: 0, done: 0, dead: 0 };\\n      for (const j of state.jobs) if (j.status in queue) queue[j.status] += 1;\\n      return json(res, 200, { ok: true, queue });\\n    }\\n    if (req.method === \\\"POST\\\" && url.pathname === \\\"/webhook/event\\\") {\\n      const body = await readBody(req);\\n      const result = acceptEvent(body);\\n      return json(res, result.ok ? 200 : 400, result);\\n    }\\n    const mApprove = url.pathname.match(/^\\\\/api\\\\/approvals\\\\/([^/]+)\\\\/approve$/);\\n    if (req.method === \\\"POST\\\" && mApprove) {\\n      const result = approve(mApprove[1]);\\n      return json(res, result.ok ? 200 : result.code, result);\\n    }\\n    const mReject = url.pathname.match(/^\\\\/api\\\\/approvals\\\\/([^/]+)\\\\/reject$/);\\n    if (req.method === \\\"POST\\\" && mReject) {\\n      const result = reject(mReject[1]);\\n      return json(res, result.ok ? 200 : result.code, result);\\n    }\\n    json(res, 404, { error: \\\"not found\\\" });\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    json(res, 400, { error: String(e.message || e) });\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nloadState();\\nsetInterval(workerTick, WORKER_MS);\\nserver.listen(PORT, () => console.log(`relay listening on :${PORT} (data: ${DATA_DIR})`));\\n// Conformance suite for Relay — the kit's permanent test bed.\\n// Runs the real server as a child process (crash recovery demands it).\\n// npm test  (= node --test tests/conformance.test.js)\\nconst { test, before, after } = require(\\\"node:test\\\");\\nconst assert = require(\\\"node:assert\\\");\\nconst { spawn } = require(\\\"node:child_process\\\");\\nconst fs = require(\\\"node:fs\\\");\\nconst path = require(\\\"node:path\\\");\\nconst os = require(\\\"node:os\\\");\\n\\nconst PORT = 4719;\\nconst BASE = `http://localhost:${PORT}`;\\nconst DATA_DIR = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \\\"relay-test-\\\"));\\nconst SERVER = path.join(__dirname, \\\"..\\\", \\\"server.js\\\");\\nlet proc;\\n\\nfunction startServer() {\\n  proc = spawn(process.execPath, [SERVER], {\\n    env: { ...process.env, PORT: String(PORT), DATA_DIR, WORKER_MS: \\\"50\\\", ALLOWLIST: \\\"test@example.com\\\" },\\n    stdio: \\\"ignore\\\",\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nasync function waitForHealth(tries = 50) {\\n  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {\\n    try {\\n      const r = await fetch(`${BASE}/health`);\\n      if (r.ok) return;\\n    } catch { /* not up yet */ }\\n    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100));\\n  }\\n  throw new Error(\\\"server did not come up\\\");\\n}\\n\\nconst post = (p, body) => fetch(BASE + p, { method: \\\"POST\\\", headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" }, body: JSON.stringify(body || {}) });\\nconst getState = async () => (await fetch(`${BASE}/api/state`)).json();\\nconst settle = async (pred, tries = 60) => {\\n  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {\\n    const s = await getState();\\n    if (pred(s)) return s;\\n    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100));\\n  }\\n  return getState();\\n};\\n\\nbefore(async () => { startServer(); await waitForHealth(); });\\nafter(() => { proc?.kill(\\\"SIGKILL\\\"); fs.rmSync(DATA_DIR, { recursive: true, force: true }); });\\n\\ntest(\\\"1. walking skeleton: event in, visible in state\\\", async () => {\\n  const r = await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e1\\\", type: \\\"meeting\\\", payload: {} });\\n  assert.strictEqual((await r.json()).ok, true);\\n  const s = await settle(x => x.events.some(e => e.id === \\\"e1\\\"));\\n  assert.ok(s.events.find(e => e.id === \\\"e1\\\"));\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"2. duplicate event id creates exactly one job\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e2\\\", payload: {} });\\n  const dup = await (await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e2\\\", payload: {} })).json();\\n  assert.strictEqual(dup.duplicate, true);\\n  const s = await getState();\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.jobs.filter(j => j.eventId === \\\"e2\\\").length, 1);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"3. transient failure retries then succeeds, attempts recorded\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e3\\\", payload: { failTimes: 2 } });\\n  const s = await settle(x => x.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e3\\\")?.status === \\\"done\\\");\\n  const job = s.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e3\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(job.status, \\\"done\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(job.attempts, 3);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"4. permanent failure dead-letters after 3 attempts\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e4\\\", payload: { failTimes: 99 } });\\n  const s = await settle(x => x.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e4\\\")?.status === \\\"dead\\\");\\n  const job = s.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e4\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(job.status, \\\"dead\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(job.attempts, 3);\\n  assert.match(job.lastError, /simulated failure/);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"5. approval gate: nothing sends before approve, sends after\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e5\\\", payload: { to: \\\"test@example.com\\\", subject: \\\"hi\\\" } });\\n  let s = await settle(x => x.approvals.some(a => a.id === \\\"appr-e5\\\"));\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.outbox.filter(o => o.approvalId === \\\"appr-e5\\\").length, 0, \\\"outbox must be empty pre-approval\\\");\\n  const r = await (await post(\\\"/api/approvals/appr-e5/approve\\\")).json();\\n  assert.strictEqual(r.ok, true);\\n  s = await getState();\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.outbox.filter(o => o.approvalId === \\\"appr-e5\\\").length, 1);\\n  // idempotent guard: second approve is refused\\n  const again = await post(\\\"/api/approvals/appr-e5/approve\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(again.status, 409);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"6. allowlist: approved send to unlisted recipient is blocked, not sent\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e6\\\", payload: { to: \\\"stranger@evil.com\\\" } });\\n  await settle(x => x.approvals.some(a => a.id === \\\"appr-e6\\\"));\\n  const r = await post(\\\"/api/approvals/appr-e6/approve\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(r.status, 403);\\n  const s = await getState();\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.approvals.find(a => a.id === \\\"appr-e6\\\").status, \\\"blocked_recipient\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.outbox.filter(o => o.approvalId === \\\"appr-e6\\\").length, 0);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"6b. reject: closes the proposal, nothing sends\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e6b\\\", payload: { to: \\\"test@example.com\\\" } });\\n  await settle(x => x.approvals.some(a => a.id === \\\"appr-e6b\\\"));\\n  const r = await (await post(\\\"/api/approvals/appr-e6b/reject\\\")).json();\\n  assert.strictEqual(r.status, \\\"rejected\\\");\\n  const s = await getState();\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.outbox.filter(o => o.approvalId === \\\"appr-e6b\\\").length, 0);\\n  // approve after reject is refused\\n  assert.strictEqual((await post(\\\"/api/approvals/appr-e6b/approve\\\")).status, 409);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"7. crash recovery: SIGKILL mid-flight loses nothing, duplicates nothing\\\", async () => {\\n  // enqueue retrying work and wait until it is PROVABLY mid-flight:\\n  // attempted at least once, not yet done. Killing before any attempt (or\\n  // after completion) would not exercise recovery.\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e7\\\", payload: { failTimes: 2, to: \\\"test@example.com\\\" } });\\n  // tight poll (10ms): the pending-with-attempts window is only ~2 worker ticks wide\\n  let midJob = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 300; i++) {\\n    const s = await getState();\\n    const j = s.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e7\\\");\\n    if (j && j.attempts >= 1 && j.status === \\\"pending\\\") { midJob = j; break; }\\n    if (j && j.status !== \\\"pending\\\") break; // completed before we caught it\\n    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 10));\\n  }\\n  assert.ok(midJob, \\\"job must be observed mid-flight (attempted, not done) at kill time\\\");\\n  proc.kill(\\\"SIGKILL\\\"); // no cleanup, no flush — the hard case\\n  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 200));\\n\\n  startServer();\\n  await waitForHealth();\\n\\n  const s = await settle(x => x.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e7\\\")?.status === \\\"done\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e7\\\").status, \\\"done\\\", \\\"pending job resumed after crash\\\");\\n  // everything from earlier tests survived\\n  assert.ok(s.events.find(e => e.id === \\\"e1\\\"), \\\"pre-crash events survived\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.outbox.filter(o => o.approvalId === \\\"appr-e5\\\").length, 1, \\\"no duplicate sends after restart\\\");\\n  // duplicate delivery after restart still refused\\n  const dup = await (await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e1\\\" })).json();\\n  assert.strictEqual(dup.duplicate, true);\\n});\\na3e0b08 T-101 tests: /health queue depth (test-author)\\nticket/T-101-health-queue-depth\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\nconformance/factory/runs/1783866071-31885.out:19:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git add -- conformance/app/tests/health.test.js && git commit -m 'T-101 tests round 2: assert HTTP 200 + pending count (test-author)' && git status --short && git show --stat --oneline --name-only HEAD\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\nconformance/factory/runs/1783866071-31885.out:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git add -- conformance/app/tests/health.test.js && git commit -m 'T-101 tests round 2: assert HTTP 200 + pending count (test-author)' && git status --short && git show --stat --oneline --name-only HEAD\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"[ticket/T-101-health-queue-depth f471404] T-101 tests round 2: assert HTTP 200 + pending count (test-author)\\n Committer: Javier Aldape <javieraldape@Javiers-Laptop.local>\\nYour name and email address were configured automatically based\\non your username and hostname. Please check that they are accurate.\\nYou can suppress this message by setting them explicitly. Run the\\nfollowing command and follow the instructions in your editor to edit\\nyour configuration file:\\n\\n    git config --global --edit\\n\\nAfter doing this, you may fix the identity used for this commit with:\\n\\n    git commit --amend --reset-author\\n\\n 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\\nf471404 T-101 tests round 2: assert HTTP 200 + pending count (test-author)\\nconformance/app/tests/health.test.js\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv:2:2026-07-12,08:03:32,T-101,test-author,codex,1,1,0.3501,0\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv:3:2026-07-12,08:06:13,T-101,builder,claude-code,1,3,0.6907800000000001,7\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv:4:2026-07-12,08:07:46,T-101,builder,claude-code,1,7,1.484044,0\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv:5:2026-07-12,08:11:42,T-101,reviewer,codex,1,1,0.7345,0\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv:6:2026-07-12,08:22:15,T-101,test-author,codex,1,1,0.2515,0\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv:7:2026-07-12,08:24:50,T-101,reviewer,codex,1,1,0.3489,0\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv:10:2026-07-12,21:06:49,T-102,test-author,codex,1,1,0.2296,0\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv:11:2026-07-12,21:10:01,T-102,builder,claude-code,1,24,0.6861495,0\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv:12:2026-07-12,21:14:32,T-102,reviewer,codex,1,1,0.1776,0\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv:13:2026-07-12,21:17:55,T-102,test-author,codex,1,1,0.1672,0\nconformance/factory/ledger.csv:14:2026-07-12,21:19:36,T-102,reviewer,codex,1,1,0.1258,0\nconformance/factory/runs/1783911942-73937.out:4:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’ll inspect the ticket, repository conventions, and branch state first. Then I’ll add only the contract-level acceptance tests, run them to verify the expected feature-missing failures, and commit just those test files.\"}}\nconformance/factory/runs/1783911942-73937.out:5:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"pwd && rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*conventions*' -g 'conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md' -g 'conformance/app/tests/**' -g 'package.json' -g 'pyproject.toml' | sed -n '1,200p' && git status --short --branch\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\nconformance/factory/runs/1783911942-73937.out:6:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"pwd && rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*conventions*' -g 'conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md' -g 'conformance/app/tests/**' -g 'package.json' -g 'pyproject.toml' | sed -n '1,200p' && git status --short --branch\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"/Users/sofiagonzalez/Projects/sf-worktrees/T-102\\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md\\nconformance/app/package.json\\nconformance/app/tests/conformance.test.js\\nconformance/app/tests/health.test.js\\n## ticket/T-102-health-approvals-summary\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\nconformance/factory/runs/1783911942-73937.out:7:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,240p' conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md && sed -n '1,260p' conformance/app/tests/health.test.js && sed -n '1,220p' conformance/app/tests/conformance.test.js && sed -n '1,200p' conformance/app/package.json && rg -n \\\\\\\"conventions|test paths|acceptance\\\\\\\" conformance/factory conformance -g '*.md' | sed -n '1,200p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\nconformance/factory/runs/1783911942-73937.out:8:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,240p' conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md && sed -n '1,260p' conformance/app/tests/health.test.js && sed -n '1,220p' conformance/app/tests/conformance.test.js && sed -n '1,200p' conformance/app/package.json && rg -n \\\\\\\"conventions|test paths|acceptance\\\\\\\" conformance/factory conformance -g '*.md' | sed -n '1,200p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# T-102 — /health reports approvals summary\\n\\nState: In progress\\nBranch: ticket/T-102-health-approvals-summary\\nRisk class: low (read-only endpoint, no external actions)\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nT-101 gave operators queue counts on `GET /health`. The other thing an operator checks at a glance is the approvals pipeline: how many proposed actions are waiting for a human, and how the closed ones ended. Extend `GET /health` to also report approvals counts by status.\\n\\nThe approval statuses in `conformance/app/server.js` are: `pending`, `sent`, `rejected`, `blocked_recipient`. The existing `ok` and `queue` fields must not change (T-101's tests stay green).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria (planner freezes the exact contract)\\n\\n1. On a fresh server, `/health` reports zero approvals in every status. → satisfied when the response body matches Frozen contract §\\\"Fresh server\\\" exactly.\\n2. After a job completes and proposes an action, `/health` shows one pending approval. → satisfied when the response body matches Frozen contract §\\\"One pending approval\\\" exactly.\\n3. After that approval is approved, `/health` shows it under sent, and pending returns to zero. → satisfied when the response body matches Frozen contract §\\\"Approved\\\" exactly.\\n\\n## Frozen contract\\n\\n`GET /health` gains an `approvals` field alongside the existing `ok` and `queue` fields (unchanged, per T-101). Response is `200 OK`, `Content-Type: application/json`.\\n\\nShape:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n  \\\"queue\\\": { \\\"pending\\\": 0, \\\"done\\\": 0, \\\"dead\\\": 0 },\\n  \\\"approvals\\\": { \\\"pending\\\": 0, \\\"sent\\\": 0, \\\"rejected\\\": 0, \\\"blocked_recipient\\\": 0 }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- `approvals` has exactly these four keys, always present, in this order, values are non-negative integers counting `state.approvals` entries by `.status` (statuses defined in `conformance/app/server.js`: `pending`, `sent`, `rejected`, `blocked_recipient`).\\n- No other keys are added to `approvals`. No existing key of the top-level response (`ok`, `queue`) changes shape or meaning.\\n\\nAcceptance criterion → exact expected body:\\n\\n1. **Fresh server** (AC1) — no events posted yet:\\n   ```json\\n   { \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"queue\\\": { \\\"pending\\\": 0, \\\"done\\\": 0, \\\"dead\\\": 0 }, \\\"approvals\\\": { \\\"pending\\\": 0, \\\"sent\\\": 0, \\\"rejected\\\": 0, \\\"blocked_recipient\\\": 0 } }\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **One pending approval** (AC2) — after posting an event and waiting for its job to reach `done` (which produces one approval in `pending`):\\n   ```json\\n   { \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"queue\\\": { \\\"pending\\\": 0, \\\"done\\\": 1, \\\"dead\\\": 0 }, \\\"approvals\\\": { \\\"pending\\\": 1, \\\"sent\\\": 0, \\\"rejected\\\": 0, \\\"blocked_recipient\\\": 0 } }\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Approved** (AC3) — after `POST /api/approvals/:id/approve` on that approval (recipient on allowlist, so it succeeds):\\n   ```json\\n   { \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"queue\\\": { \\\"pending\\\": 0, \\\"done\\\": 1, \\\"dead\\\": 0 }, \\\"approvals\\\": { \\\"pending\\\": 0, \\\"sent\\\": 1, \\\"rejected\\\": 0, \\\"blocked_recipient\\\": 0 } }\\n   ```\\n\\nIf this contract proves wrong during build or test-authoring, the ticket goes back to Ready for re-planning as a new version — do not silently change the shape.\\n\\n## Conventions\\n\\n- App lives in `conformance/app/` (zero-dependency Node 18+; see `conformance/SPEC.md`).\\n- Tests go in `conformance/app/tests/` — new file `tests/health-approvals.test.js`, same style as the existing suites (node:test, spawn the real server on its own port with a temp DATA_DIR).\\n- Run tests from `conformance/app/` with `node --test tests/health-approvals.test.js`.\\n\\n## Log\\n\\n- 2026-07-12: ticket created by the operator; State → Ready. First ticket to be dispatched by Hermes (dispatcher trial).\\n- 2026-07-12: planner froze `GET /health` `approvals` contract and mapped acceptance criteria to exact response bodies.\\n- 2026-07-12 21:01:57: planner run completed through the wrapper; contract frozen in commit `8f0bc25`; State → In progress; cost $0.3306252.\\nconst { test, before, after } = require(\\\"node:test\\\");\\nconst assert = require(\\\"node:assert\\\");\\nconst { spawn } = require(\\\"node:child_process\\\");\\nconst fs = require(\\\"node:fs\\\");\\nconst path = require(\\\"node:path\\\");\\nconst os = require(\\\"node:os\\\");\\n\\nconst PORT = 4721;\\nconst BASE = `http://localhost:${PORT}`;\\nconst DATA_DIR = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \\\"relay-health-test-\\\"));\\nconst SERVER = path.join(__dirname, \\\"..\\\", \\\"server.js\\\");\\nlet proc;\\n\\nconst post = (body) => fetch(`${BASE}/webhook/event`, {\\n  method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n  headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n  body: JSON.stringify(body),\\n});\\nconst getHealth = async () => (await fetch(`${BASE}/health`)).json();\\nconst getState = async () => (await fetch(`${BASE}/api/state`)).json();\\n\\nasync function settle(pred, tries = 60) {\\n  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {\\n    const state = await getState();\\n    if (pred(state)) return;\\n    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\\n  }\\n  throw new Error(\\\"job did not settle\\\");\\n}\\n\\nbefore(async () => {\\n  proc = spawn(process.execPath, [SERVER], {\\n    env: { ...process.env, PORT: String(PORT), DATA_DIR, WORKER_MS: \\\"50\\\" },\\n    stdio: \\\"ignore\\\",\\n  });\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\\n    try {\\n      if ((await fetch(`${BASE}/health`)).ok) return;\\n    } catch { /* not up yet */ }\\n    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\\n  }\\n  throw new Error(\\\"server did not come up\\\");\\n});\\n\\nafter(() => {\\n  proc?.kill(\\\"SIGKILL\\\");\\n  fs.rmSync(DATA_DIR, { recursive: true, force: true });\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"1. on a fresh server, /health reports an empty queue\\\", async () => {\\n  const response = await fetch(`${BASE}/health`);\\n  assert.strictEqual(response.status, 200);\\n  assert.deepStrictEqual(await response.json(), {\\n    ok: true,\\n    queue: { pending: 0, done: 0, dead: 0 },\\n  });\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"1b. after an event is accepted, /health reports queue.pending incremented by 1\\\", async () => {\\n  const pendingPort = 4722;\\n  const pendingBase = `http://localhost:${pendingPort}`;\\n  const pendingDataDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \\\"relay-health-pending-test-\\\"));\\n  const pendingProc = spawn(process.execPath, [SERVER], {\\n    env: { ...process.env, PORT: String(pendingPort), DATA_DIR: pendingDataDir, WORKER_MS: \\\"600000\\\" },\\n    stdio: \\\"ignore\\\",\\n  });\\n\\n  try {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\\n      try {\\n        if ((await fetch(`${pendingBase}/health`)).ok) break;\\n      } catch { /* not up yet */ }\\n      if (i === 49) throw new Error(\\\"pending server did not come up\\\");\\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\\n    }\\n\\n    await fetch(`${pendingBase}/webhook/event`, {\\n      method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n      headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n      body: JSON.stringify({ id: \\\"health-pending\\\", payload: {} }),\\n    });\\n\\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(await (await fetch(`${pendingBase}/health`)).json(), {\\n      ok: true,\\n      queue: { pending: 1, done: 0, dead: 0 },\\n    });\\n  } finally {\\n    pendingProc.kill(\\\"SIGKILL\\\");\\n    fs.rmSync(pendingDataDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\\n  }\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"2. after a job completes, /health reports queue.done incremented by 1\\\", async () => {\\n  await post({ id: \\\"health-done\\\", payload: {} });\\n  await settle(state => state.jobs.find(job => job.eventId === \\\"health-done\\\")?.status === \\\"done\\\");\\n\\n  assert.deepStrictEqual(await getHealth(), {\\n    ok: true,\\n    queue: { pending: 0, done: 1, dead: 0 },\\n  });\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"3. after a job exhausts retries, /health reports queue.dead incremented by 1\\\", async () => {\\n  await post({ id: \\\"health-dead\\\", payload: { failTimes: 99 } });\\n  await settle(state => state.jobs.find(job => job.eventId === \\\"health-dead\\\")?.status === \\\"dead\\\");\\n\\n  assert.deepStrictEqual(await getHealth(), {\\n    ok: true,\\n    queue: { pending: 0, done: 1, dead: 1 },\\n  });\\n});\\n// Conformance suite for Relay — the kit's permanent test bed.\\n// Runs the real server as a child process (crash recovery demands it).\\n// npm test  (= node --test tests/conformance.test.js)\\nconst { test, before, after } = require(\\\"node:test\\\");\\nconst assert = require(\\\"node:assert\\\");\\nconst { spawn } = require(\\\"node:child_process\\\");\\nconst fs = require(\\\"node:fs\\\");\\nconst path = require(\\\"node:path\\\");\\nconst os = require(\\\"node:os\\\");\\n\\nconst PORT = 4719;\\nconst BASE = `http://localhost:${PORT}`;\\nconst DATA_DIR = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \\\"relay-test-\\\"));\\nconst SERVER = path.join(__dirname, \\\"..\\\", \\\"server.js\\\");\\nlet proc;\\n\\nfunction startServer() {\\n  proc = spawn(process.execPath, [SERVER], {\\n    env: { ...process.env, PORT: String(PORT), DATA_DIR, WORKER_MS: \\\"50\\\", ALLOWLIST: \\\"test@example.com\\\" },\\n    stdio: \\\"ignore\\\",\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nasync function waitForHealth(tries = 50) {\\n  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {\\n    try {\\n      const r = await fetch(`${BASE}/health`);\\n      if (r.ok) return;\\n    } catch { /* not up yet */ }\\n    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100));\\n  }\\n  throw new Error(\\\"server did not come up\\\");\\n}\\n\\nconst post = (p, body) => fetch(BASE + p, { method: \\\"POST\\\", headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" }, body: JSON.stringify(body || {}) });\\nconst getState = async () => (await fetch(`${BASE}/api/state`)).json();\\nconst settle = async (pred, tries = 60) => {\\n  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {\\n    const s = await getState();\\n    if (pred(s)) return s;\\n    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100));\\n  }\\n  return getState();\\n};\\n\\nbefore(async () => { startServer(); await waitForHealth(); });\\nafter(() => { proc?.kill(\\\"SIGKILL\\\"); fs.rmSync(DATA_DIR, { recursive: true, force: true }); });\\n\\ntest(\\\"1. walking skeleton: event in, visible in state\\\", async () => {\\n  const r = await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e1\\\", type: \\\"meeting\\\", payload: {} });\\n  assert.strictEqual((await r.json()).ok, true);\\n  const s = await settle(x => x.events.some(e => e.id === \\\"e1\\\"));\\n  assert.ok(s.events.find(e => e.id === \\\"e1\\\"));\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"2. duplicate event id creates exactly one job\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e2\\\", payload: {} });\\n  const dup = await (await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e2\\\", payload: {} })).json();\\n  assert.strictEqual(dup.duplicate, true);\\n  const s = await getState();\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.jobs.filter(j => j.eventId === \\\"e2\\\").length, 1);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"3. transient failure retries then succeeds, attempts recorded\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e3\\\", payload: { failTimes: 2 } });\\n  const s = await settle(x => x.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e3\\\")?.status === \\\"done\\\");\\n  const job = s.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e3\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(job.status, \\\"done\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(job.attempts, 3);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"4. permanent failure dead-letters after 3 attempts\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e4\\\", payload: { failTimes: 99 } });\\n  const s = await settle(x => x.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e4\\\")?.status === \\\"dead\\\");\\n  const job = s.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e4\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(job.status, \\\"dead\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(job.attempts, 3);\\n  assert.match(job.lastError, /simulated failure/);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"5. approval gate: nothing sends before approve, sends after\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e5\\\", payload: { to: \\\"test@example.com\\\", subject: \\\"hi\\\" } });\\n  let s = await settle(x => x.approvals.some(a => a.id === \\\"appr-e5\\\"));\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.outbox.filter(o => o.approvalId === \\\"appr-e5\\\").length, 0, \\\"outbox must be empty pre-approval\\\");\\n  const r = await (await post(\\\"/api/approvals/appr-e5/approve\\\")).json();\\n  assert.strictEqual(r.ok, true);\\n  s = await getState();\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.outbox.filter(o => o.approvalId === \\\"appr-e5\\\").length, 1);\\n  // idempotent guard: second approve is refused\\n  const again = await post(\\\"/api/approvals/appr-e5/approve\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(again.status, 409);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"6. allowlist: approved send to unlisted recipient is blocked, not sent\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e6\\\", payload: { to: \\\"stranger@evil.com\\\" } });\\n  await settle(x => x.approvals.some(a => a.id === \\\"appr-e6\\\"));\\n  const r = await post(\\\"/api/approvals/appr-e6/approve\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(r.status, 403);\\n  const s = await getState();\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.approvals.find(a => a.id === \\\"appr-e6\\\").status, \\\"blocked_recipient\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.outbox.filter(o => o.approvalId === \\\"appr-e6\\\").length, 0);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"6b. reject: closes the proposal, nothing sends\\\", async () => {\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e6b\\\", payload: { to: \\\"test@example.com\\\" } });\\n  await settle(x => x.approvals.some(a => a.id === \\\"appr-e6b\\\"));\\n  const r = await (await post(\\\"/api/approvals/appr-e6b/reject\\\")).json();\\n  assert.strictEqual(r.status, \\\"rejected\\\");\\n  const s = await getState();\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.outbox.filter(o => o.approvalId === \\\"appr-e6b\\\").length, 0);\\n  // approve after reject is refused\\n  assert.strictEqual((await post(\\\"/api/approvals/appr-e6b/approve\\\")).status, 409);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"7. crash recovery: SIGKILL mid-flight loses nothing, duplicates nothing\\\", async () => {\\n  // enqueue retrying work and wait until it is PROVABLY mid-flight:\\n  // attempted at least once, not yet done. Killing before any attempt (or\\n  // after completion) would not exercise recovery.\\n  await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e7\\\", payload: { failTimes: 2, to: \\\"test@example.com\\\" } });\\n  // tight poll (10ms): the pending-with-attempts window is only ~2 worker ticks wide\\n  let midJob = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 300; i++) {\\n    const s = await getState();\\n    const j = s.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e7\\\");\\n    if (j && j.attempts >= 1 && j.status === \\\"pending\\\") { midJob = j; break; }\\n    if (j && j.status !== \\\"pending\\\") break; // completed before we caught it\\n    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 10));\\n  }\\n  assert.ok(midJob, \\\"job must be observed mid-flight (attempted, not done) at kill time\\\");\\n  proc.kill(\\\"SIGKILL\\\"); // no cleanup, no flush — the hard case\\n  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 200));\\n\\n  startServer();\\n  await waitForHealth();\\n\\n  const s = await settle(x => x.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e7\\\")?.status === \\\"done\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.jobs.find(j => j.eventId === \\\"e7\\\").status, \\\"done\\\", \\\"pending job resumed after crash\\\");\\n  // everything from earlier tests survived\\n  assert.ok(s.events.find(e => e.id === \\\"e1\\\"), \\\"pre-crash events survived\\\");\\n  assert.strictEqual(s.outbox.filter(o => o.approvalId === \\\"appr-e5\\\").length, 1, \\\"no duplicate sends after restart\\\");\\n  // duplicate delivery after restart still refused\\n  const dup = await (await post(\\\"/webhook/event\\\", { id: \\\"e1\\\" })).json();\\n  assert.strictEqual(dup.duplicate, true);\\n});\\n{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"relay-conformance\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Nysa-shaped conformance product for the software factory kit. Zero dependencies.\\\",\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"start\\\": \\\"node server.js\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"node --test tests/conformance.test.js\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:64:- 2026-07-12: planner froze `GET /health` `approvals` contract and mapped acceptance criteria to exact response bodies.\\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:64:- 2026-07-12: planner froze `GET /health` `approvals` contract and mapped acceptance criteria to exact response bodies.\\nconformance/SHAKEDOWN-REPORT.md:48:The enforcement layer now holds against its own reviewers' attacks: no identity-based bypasses, anchored kill switch, reservation-based caps, mechanical cross-family and approval rules. Conformance suite: 8/8 green. Remaining honest gap, unchanged: **no ticket has yet run with real (non-mock) CLI agents** — that first real run is what the operator go-ahead buys, and it is the kit's final acceptance test.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\nconformance/factory/runs/1783911942-73937.out:11:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,280p' conformance/app/server.js && git log --oneline --decorate -8 && git status --porcelain=v1\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"// Relay — conformance product. Zero dependencies; Node 18+.\\n// See ../SPEC.md for the behavior contract this implements.\\nconst http = require(\\\"node:http\\\");\\nconst fs = require(\\\"node:fs\\\");\\nconst path = require(\\\"node:path\\\");\\nconst crypto = require(\\\"node:crypto\\\");\\n\\nconst PORT = Number(process.env.PORT || 4700);\\nconst DATA_DIR = process.env.DATA_DIR || path.join(__dirname, \\\"data\\\");\\nconst STATE_FILE = path.join(DATA_DIR, \\\"state.json\\\");\\nconst ALLOWLIST = (process.env.ALLOWLIST || \\\"test@example.com\\\").split(\\\",\\\").map(s => s.trim());\\nconst WORKER_MS = Number(process.env.WORKER_MS || 200);\\nconst MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3;\\n\\n// ---------- durable state ----------\\nlet state = { events: [], jobs: [], approvals: [], outbox: [] };\\n\\nfunction loadState() {\\n  try {\\n    state = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(STATE_FILE, \\\"utf8\\\"));\\n  } catch {\\n    /* first boot or unreadable: start clean */\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Atomic persist: write temp file, then rename. A crash mid-write never\\n// corrupts the previous good state.\\nfunction persist() {\\n  fs.mkdirSync(DATA_DIR, { recursive: true });\\n  const tmp = STATE_FILE + \\\".\\\" + crypto.randomBytes(4).toString(\\\"hex\\\");\\n  fs.writeFileSync(tmp, JSON.stringify(state, null, 2));\\n  fs.renameSync(tmp, STATE_FILE);\\n}\\n\\n// ---------- domain ----------\\nfunction acceptEvent(evt) {\\n  if (!evt || typeof evt.id !== \\\"string\\\" || !evt.id) return { ok: false, error: \\\"missing event id\\\" };\\n  const existing = state.events.find(e => e.id === evt.id);\\n  if (existing) return { ok: true, duplicate: true, eventId: evt.id }; // idempotent ack\\n  state.events.push({ id: evt.id, type: evt.type || \\\"generic\\\", payload: evt.payload || {}, receivedAt: new Date().toISOString() });\\n  state.jobs.push({\\n    id: \\\"job-\\\" + evt.id,\\n    eventId: evt.id,\\n    status: \\\"pending\\\", // pending | done | dead\\n    attempts: 0,\\n    lastError: null,\\n  });\\n  persist();\\n  return { ok: true, duplicate: false, eventId: evt.id };\\n}\\n\\nfunction processJob(job) {\\n  const evt = state.events.find(e => e.id === job.eventId);\\n  job.attempts += 1;\\n  // Simulated transient/permanent failure: payload.failTimes = number of\\n  // attempts that must fail before success (99 = effectively permanent).\\n  const failTimes = Number(evt?.payload?.failTimes || 0);\\n  if (job.attempts <= failTimes) {\\n    job.lastError = `simulated failure on attempt ${job.attempts}`;\\n    if (job.attempts >= MAX_ATTEMPTS) job.status = \\\"dead\\\";\\n    persist();\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  // Success: produce a proposed action requiring approval. Nothing sends here.\\n  state.approvals.push({\\n    id: \\\"appr-\\\" + job.eventId,\\n    jobId: job.id,\\n    action: {\\n      to: evt?.payload?.to || ALLOWLIST[0],\\n      subject: evt?.payload?.subject || `Follow-up for ${job.eventId}`,\\n      body: evt?.payload?.body || \\\"Proposed by Relay worker.\\\",\\n    },\\n    status: \\\"pending\\\", // pending | sent | rejected | blocked_recipient\\n    proposedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\\n  });\\n  job.status = \\\"done\\\";\\n  job.lastError = null;\\n  persist();\\n}\\n\\nfunction workerTick() {\\n  const job = state.jobs.find(j => j.status === \\\"pending\\\");\\n  if (job) processJob(job);\\n}\\n\\nfunction approve(id) {\\n  const appr = state.approvals.find(a => a.id === id);\\n  if (!appr) return { ok: false, code: 404, error: \\\"no such approval\\\" };\\n  if (appr.status !== \\\"pending\\\") return { ok: false, code: 409, error: `already ${appr.status}` };\\n  if (!ALLOWLIST.includes(appr.action.to)) {\\n    appr.status = \\\"blocked_recipient\\\";\\n    persist();\\n    return { ok: false, code: 403, error: `recipient ${appr.action.to} not on allowlist — send blocked`, status: appr.status };\\n  }\\n  state.outbox.push({ ...appr.action, approvalId: appr.id, sentAt: new Date().toISOString() });\\n  appr.status = \\\"sent\\\";\\n  persist();\\n  return { ok: true, status: \\\"sent\\\" };\\n}\\n\\nfunction reject(id) {\\n  const appr = state.approvals.find(a => a.id === id);\\n  if (!appr) return { ok: false, code: 404, error: \\\"no such approval\\\" };\\n  if (appr.status !== \\\"pending\\\") return { ok: false, code: 409, error: `already ${appr.status}` };\\n  appr.status = \\\"rejected\\\";\\n  persist();\\n  return { ok: true, status: \\\"rejected\\\" };\\n}\\n\\n// ---------- http ----------\\nfunction json(res, code, obj) {\\n  res.writeHead(code, { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" });\\n  res.end(JSON.stringify(obj));\\n}\\n\\nfunction readBody(req) {\\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n    let data = \\\"\\\";\\n    req.on(\\\"data\\\", c => { data += c; if (data.length > 1e6) req.destroy(); });\\n    req.on(\\\"end\\\", () => { try { resolve(data ? JSON.parse(data) : {}); } catch (e) { reject(e); } });\\n    req.on(\\\"error\\\", reject);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nfunction ui() {\\n  const row = (cells) => `<tr>${cells.map(c => `<td>${String(c)}</td>`).join(\\\"\\\")}</tr>`;\\n  return `<!doctype html><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\"><title>Relay</title>\\n<style>body{font-family:system-ui;margin:2rem;max-width:60rem}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:1.5rem}td,th{border:1px solid #ddd;padding:.4rem .6rem;text-align:left;font-size:14px}h2{margin:.2rem 0 .4rem}</style>\\n<h1>Relay</h1>\\n<h2>Events (${state.events.length})</h2><table><tr><th>id</th><th>type</th><th>received</th></tr>${state.events.map(e => row([e.id, e.type, e.receivedAt])).join(\\\"\\\")}</table>\\n<h2>Jobs</h2><table><tr><th>id</th><th>status</th><th>attempts</th><th>lastError</th></tr>${state.jobs.map(j => row([j.id, j.status, j.attempts, j.lastError || \\\"\\\"])).join(\\\"\\\")}</table>\\n<h2>Approvals</h2><table><tr><th>id</th><th>to</th><th>subject</th><th>status</th></tr>${state.approvals.map(a => row([a.id, a.action.to, a.action.subject, a.status])).join(\\\"\\\")}</table>\\n<h2>Outbox (sandboxed)</h2><table><tr><th>to</th><th>subject</th><th>sentAt</th></tr>${state.outbox.map(o => row([o.to, o.subject, o.sentAt])).join(\\\"\\\")}</table>`;\\n}\\n\\nconst server = http.createServer(async (req, res) => {\\n  const url = new URL(req.url, `http://localhost:${PORT}`);\\n  try {\\n    if (req.method === \\\"GET\\\" && url.pathname === \\\"/\\\") {\\n      res.writeHead(200, { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"text/html\\\" });\\n      return res.end(ui());\\n    }\\n    if (req.method === \\\"GET\\\" && url.pathname === \\\"/api/state\\\") return json(res, 200, state);\\n    if (req.method === \\\"GET\\\" && url.pathname === \\\"/health\\\") {\\n      const queue = { pending: 0, done: 0, dead: 0 };\\n      for (const j of state.jobs) if (j.status in queue) queue[j.status] += 1;\\n      return json(res, 200, { ok: true, queue });\\n    }\\n    if (req.method === \\\"POST\\\" && url.pathname === \\\"/webhook/event\\\") {\\n      const body = await readBody(req);\\n      const result = acceptEvent(body);\\n      return json(res, result.ok ? 200 : 400, result);\\n    }\\n    const mApprove = url.pathname.match(/^\\\\/api\\\\/approvals\\\\/([^/]+)\\\\/approve$/);\\n    if (req.method === \\\"POST\\\" && mApprove) {\\n      const result = approve(mApprove[1]);\\n      return json(res, result.ok ? 200 : result.code, result);\\n    }\\n    const mReject = url.pathname.match(/^\\\\/api\\\\/approvals\\\\/([^/]+)\\\\/reject$/);\\n    if (req.method === \\\"POST\\\" && mReject) {\\n      const result = reject(mReject[1]);\\n      return json(res, result.ok ? 200 : result.code, result);\\n    }\\n    json(res, 404, { error: \\\"not found\\\" });\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    json(res, 400, { error: String(e.message || e) });\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nloadState();\\nsetInterval(workerTick, WORKER_MS);\\nserver.listen(PORT, () => console.log(`relay listening on :${PORT} (data: ${DATA_DIR})`));\\n5ed8491 (HEAD -> ticket/T-102-health-approvals-summary) Log T-102 planner completion\\n8f0bc25 T-102: freeze GET /health approvals contract\\nba83735 (origin/main, origin/HEAD, main) Phase 2: next-stage.sh mechanical sequencer (dispatcher v2 must obey it; reviewer verdicts required on ticket) + machine-level global daily cap across factories in run-agent.sh\\nf32a804 Branch protection rewritten from live probes: rulesets not classic protection; deploy keys bypass classic and role-based bypasses; org-admin-only bypass; probe procedure documented\\ne22a462 protection probe (should be rejected)\\n63b106b T-102 in Ready for the Hermes dispatcher trial; branch-protection doc: sole-operator admin exemption\\n6b4b7e6 CI smoke run after org transfer\\nf18f691 Hermes dispatcher trial prep: live CI workflow + dispatcher role prompt (four verbs, wrapper-only, no merge rights)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:53:If this contract proves wrong during build or test-authoring, the ticket goes back to Ready for re-planning as a new version — do not silently change the shape.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:66:- 2026-07-12 21:06:49: test-author run completed through the wrapper; 3 contract tests committed in `18a7731`, all failing for the expected missing `approvals` field (0 passed, 3 failed); cost $0.2296.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:67:- 2026-07-12: builder implemented the frozen contract exactly (added `approvals` counts to the `/health` handler in `conformance/app/server.js`). `tests/health-approvals.test.js` (3/3) passes with exact `JSON.stringify` matches, confirming the implementation matches the frozen contract. **Blocked before commit:** this breaks all 4 pre-existing T-101 tests in `tests/health.test.js` (tests 1, 1b, 2, 3), which assert the `/health` body with `assert.deepStrictEqual(...)` against object literals that have no `approvals` key — `deepStrictEqual` rejects any extra key, so adding `approvals` anywhere in the response necessarily fails them. This is not an implementation bug: no server-side change can satisfy both \"exact frozen `approvals` shape per AC1–3\" and \"T-101's `health.test.js` stays green,\" because the latter was written before this contract existed and asserts an exact object with no extra keys. Per the builder's no-test-editing rule, I have not touched `tests/health.test.js` or any other test file, and have not committed the (correct, but suite-red) implementation change. Flagging for re-planning/reviewer adjudication: either (a) the contract stands and `health.test.js`'s 4 assertions need updating by the test-author/reviewer