 after exactly 3 new attempts, with cumulative attempts visible on the record (964.971375ms)\n✔ 3. Retry of a non-dead job (pending or done) → refused with 409, record unchanged (227.456375ms)\n✔ 4. Kill the server right after a retry is accepted; on restart the re-queued job is processed (3357.01075ms)\n✔ Unknown job → 404 with exactly the frozen no-such-job response (111.387375ms)\nℹ tests 25\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 25\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 5541.860917\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"REQUEST CHANGES — round 2\n\n1. Commit `66cde3e` changes acceptance tests after implementation commit `aefdef1`, violating the test-immutability ordering convention. The configured CI command rejects it under rule 2. Reorder the corrected test commit before implementation, preserving content, then rerun CI.\n\nThe two requested test gaps are correctly resolved, the implementation matches the frozen contract, and independent runs pass targeted 5/5 and full suite 25/25. Because this is round 2, move T-104 to Blocked-Escalated. The operator can either authorize history reordering or explicitly waive/change the immutability rule; I recommend reordering the commits because it preserves both the corrected tests and the existing convention."}}
